<title>MEXICO: Mexico's nominal GDP 2.544 trillion pesos in 1996.</title>
<headline>Mexico's nominal GDP 2.544 trillion pesos in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's nominal gross domestic product at market prices was 2.544 trillion current pesos in 1996, and the implicit price deflator was 31.5 percent in 1996 versus 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It reaffirmed data released last week showing the economy grew 5.1 percent in 1996 compared to the year before.</p>
<p>INEGI released the following data on nominal GDP:</p>
<p>Sector	    Amount in current prices	   Percentage</p>
<p>			     bln pesos	     of total nominal</p>
<p>GDP</p>
<p>Farming,</p>
<p>Forestry and Fishing     136.595			5.9 pct</p>
<p>Industrial:		  668.495		     28.8 pct</p>
<p>  Mining			42.006			1.8 pct</p>
<p>  Manufacturing	    499.525		     21.5 pct</p>
<p>  Construction		98.336			4.3 pct</p>
<p>Power Generation</p>
<p>  Electricity, Gas, Water 28.628			1.2 pct</p>
<p>Commerce, Restaurants,</p>
<p>Hotels			 489.910		     21.1 pct</p>
<p>Services		   1,027.285		     44.2 pct</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
